 incorrect or invalid you can see  exactly  when you used it and how it affected  your decision and can go back  or theoretically go back and and change  um the course of action that you would  take or identify if  a change is necessary uh context manager  this one's talked about a lot where  somebody has all of the information  and they only pass on to the analysts  what is  necessary for their for their task at  that particular point  uh independent checking or review this  is another  uh one where which most  most practitioners i talk to have some  form of review  whereby it may be administrative or  technical  um somehow on every case some will do on  a proportion of cases  and the independent part of it is trying  to recognize that  the reviewer may be influenced by what  the first examiner has said  so is it possible you know if the  reviewer  is um  is looking at the case that they already  know how the number of contributors that  you've determined  um in a sample  well does that then influence how they  move forward with reviewing the case or  is it better for them not to know that  at all  and to try and come up with that on  their own is that a more  appropriate way of really reviewing and  assessing the initial examination  so there's quite a few different options  here and i'm not going to go through  them all because  it really depends on what discipline  you're in what the task is what  uh your agency kind of setup is like  but i'm more than happy for anyone to  contact me later on and i can  talk through various options uh specific  to your situation  and what we know is that there are  benefits  of contextual information management  beyond just minimizing bias  so you may be of the view that bias is  not so much of an issue for you or in  your agency but  there are benefits um to implementing  this  first and foremost maintains  transparency and integrity in the  decision making process  by mapping decision points you can  identify  potential areas 