ts of  the system  that humans make decisions within  and it may not just be are you biased  when looking at the specific evidence  but how reliable and valid are your  opinions in general  is the discipline in general  and what's the efficacy of training and  competency standards  so these are things that are being  looked at by various groups  for example the role of management  creating a positive aeroculture  impact of wording and statements process  mapping  and in osak the organization of  scientific area committees  um there is a designated committee this  human factors  committee that is embedded into every  discipline to try and understand some of  these issues  as well as minus but thinking much  further beyond that  uh and most along with nij  uh have expert working groups  in human factors for various disciplines  and their role really is to understand  the entire system and how  uh the human side of that can be  improved for yeah for safer justice  outcomes  so thank you for sticking it out if you  have  uh and these are my contact details  i'm more than happy if anyone would like  to reach out and ask any questions  uh if you have any particular  concerns within your own lab uh or if  you  you know are interested in in looking at  contextual information management then  please do reach out and happy to answer  any questions  and i think i'm just about on 30 minutes  i hope that you've managed to stick it  out and  that you're all home safe and well thank  you very much
 

